{
  "tema": 6869,
  "slug": "tenia-tuvo",
  "titulo": "Tener in the imperfect vs the preterite",
  "subtitulo": "Tenía un carro / Tuvo un accidente.",
  "foto": "t05.jpg",
  "regla": "Tenía = had (possession or state as background, no limits). Tuvo = had in a closed period, or got / received / had an event: tuvo un bebé, tuve un examen, tuvo un accidente.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": "2026-10-10",
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "tabla",
          "encabezados": [
            "Form",
            "Meaning",
            "Example"
          ],
          "filas": [
            [
              "tenía",
              "had: background possession or state",
              "Marcos tenía un carro nuevo."
            ],
            [
              "tuvo",
              "had something happen, got, received; or had it for a finished period",
              "Tuvo un accidente. Tuve ese carro diez años."
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "With the preterite, **tener** often becomes an **event**: **tuvo un bebé** (_she had a baby_), **tuve una idea**, **tuvimos una junta**, **tuve noticias de él**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Tener que** follows the same logic: **tenía que ir** (_I was supposed to go_; did I?) vs **tuve que ir** (_I had to go, and I went_)."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: **tenía** is owning; **tuvo** is something happening."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "pares",
          "lista": [
            {
              "filas": [
                {
                  "v": "tenía",
                  "t": "El pueblo tenía muchos visitantes."
                },
                {
                  "v": "tuvo",
                  "t": "El pueblo tuvo muchos visitantes ese verano."
                }
              ],
              "nota": "**Tuvo**: a closed period, now it's different."
            },
            {
              "filas": [
                {
                  "v": "tenía que",
                  "t": "Tenía que trabajar, pero me quedé en casa."
                },
                {
                  "v": "tuve que",
                  "t": "Tuve que trabajar el domingo."
                }
              ],
              "nota": "**Tuve que**: it happened."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "Mi hermana ==tuvo== gemelos.",
              "en": "My sister had twins."
            },
            {
              "es": "Ayer ==tuve== un examen de química.",
              "en": "Yesterday I had a chemistry exam."
            },
            {
              "es": "De niño ==tenía== un perro que se llamaba Chispas.",
              "en": "As a kid I had a dog called Chispas."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Tuvimos== que esperar dos horas.",
              "en": "We had to wait two hours."
            }
